      "content": "#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <climits>\n\nclass FastScanner {\n    static const int BUFSIZE = 1 << 20;\n    char buf[BUFSIZE];\n    int idx, size;\npublic:\n    FastScanner() : idx(0), size(0) {}\n    inline char getChar() {\n        if (idx >= size) {\n            size = fread(buf, 1, BUFSIZE, stdin);\n            idx = 0;\n            if (size == 0) return 0;\n        }\n        return buf[idx++];\n    }\n    int nextInt() {\n        char c;\n        do { c = getChar(); } while (c <= ' ');\n        int sign = 1;\n        if (c == '-') { sign = -1; c = getChar(); }\n        int x = 0;\n        while (c > ' ') {\n            x = x * 10 + (c - '0');\n            c = getChar();\n        }\n        return x * sign;\n    }\n};\n\nint main() {\n    FastScanner fs;\n    int n = fs.nextInt();\n    int s = fs.nextInt();\n\n    const int N = n + 1;\n    std::vector<long long> P(N * N, 0);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            int val = fs.nextInt();\n            P[(i + 1) * N + (j + 1)] = val + P[i * N + (j + 1)] + P[(i + 1) * N + j] - P[i * N + j];\n        }\n    }\n\n    long long mxSum = LLONG_MIN;\n    int limit_i = n - s;\n    int limit_j = n - s;\n\n    #pragma omp parallel for reduction(max:mxSum)\n    for (int i = 0; i <= limit_i; ++i) {\n        long long rowBest = LLONG_MIN;\n        const long long* base1 = &P[i * N];\n        const long long* base2 = &P[(i + s) * N];\n        #pragma omp simd reduction(max:rowBest)\n        for (int j = 0; j <= limit_j; ++j) {\n            long long sum = base2[j + s] - base1[j + s] - base2[j] + base1[j];\n            rowBest = std::max(rowBest, sum);\n        }\n        mxSum = std::max(mxSum, rowBest);\n    }\n\n    printf(\"%lld\\n\", mxSum);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Replacing the original O(S*N^2) sliding-window traversal with a 2D prefix-sum formulation makes every SxS submatrix sum computable in O(1). This yields an O(N^2) algorithm whose inner loop over starting columns is fully independent, allowing legal SIMD vectorization via omp simd reduction(max) and parallelization across rows via OpenMP. Combined with a custom fread-based scanner to eliminate I/O overhead, this should significantly reduce runtime while preserving exact output.",
  "notes": "Uses long long for prefix sums to avoid signed overflow; final result fits int but printed as %lld. The inner loop is vectorizable because each sum depends only on four independent loads from the prefix array. OpenMP reduction(max) handles thread combination correctly. No changes to input/output contract or resource limits.",
